---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Data Methodology - IPOFins',
  description:
    'How IPOFins sources, processes, and publishes IPO, mutual fund, and market data for Indian investors.',
  url: 'https://ipofins.com/methodology',
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Data Methodology — How IPOFins Sources & Processes Data"
  description="How IPOFins collects IPO, mutual fund NAV, shareholding pattern (SHP), SAST, and monthly holdings data from SEBI, AMFI, NSE, and BSE disclosures."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="container-narrow py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary-600 dark:text-primary-400">
        Transparency
      </p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl lg:text-4xl font-extrabold text-surface-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
        How We Source Data
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-300 leading-relaxed">
        IPOFins is built on publicly available regulatory and exchange disclosures. We do not repackage
        unofficial indicators such as grey market premium (GMP). Our goal is to make official data
        easier to search, compare, and understand.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-300 leading-relaxed">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900 dark:text-white">IPO Data</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            IPO timelines, price bands, lot sizes, subscription status, and listing performance are
            compiled from authorized sources including <strong class="text-surface-800 dark:text-surface-100">SEBI</strong>,{' '}
            <strong class="text-surface-800 dark:text-surface-100">NSE</strong>, and{' '}
            <strong class="text-surface-800 dark:text-surface-100">BSE</strong> filings and exchange
            disclosures. Subscription figures are shown only when officially published.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900 dark:text-white">Mutual Fund NAV</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Fund names, categories, and NAV history are sourced from{' '}
            <strong class="text-surface-800 dark:text-surface-100">AMFI India</strong> daily NAV
            disclosures. We focus on Direct-Growth plans where applicable for fair comparison.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900 dark:text-white">Monthly Holdings &amp; Changes</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Mutual fund portfolio holdings are parsed from monthly AMC disclosure files published on
            fund house websites, as mandated by SEBI. IPOFins normalizes fund names across AMCs,
            deduplicates overlapping files, and computes month-over-month additions, removals, and
            weight changes. Coverage grows as new AMC files are processed each month.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900 dark:text-white">IPOFins Score</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Where shown, the IPOFins Score is a quantitative rating based on available financials,
            valuation context, sector data, and issue structure. It is a research aid—not a buy or
            sell recommendation. Scores are only displayed when sufficient data is available.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900 dark:text-white">Shareholding Pattern (SHP)</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Quarterly shareholding pattern filings published on{' '}
            <strong class="text-surface-800 dark:text-surface-100">NSE</strong> and{' '}
            <strong class="text-surface-800 dark:text-surface-100">BSE</strong> list every shareholder
            owning 1% or more of a company (excluding promoters in our 1% Club view). IPOFins parses these
            XML/PDF disclosures to build per-stock holder lists and links them to curated investor profiles
            where names can be reliably matched.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900 dark:text-white">1% Club</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The <a href="/1-percent-club" class="text-primary-600 dark:text-primary-400 hover:underline">1% Club</a>{' '}
            shows all non-promoter shareholders at or above the 1% threshold for each covered stock.
            Holders matched to a curated super-investor profile are labelled; unmatched names appear as
            &ldquo;mystery&rdquo; holders until entity resolution improves. Stake percentages and quarter
            labels reflect the latest parsed SHP filing for that stock.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900 dark:text-white">Super Investors &amp; Entity Resolution</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Our <a href="/super-investors" class="text-primary-600 dark:text-primary-400 hover:underline">Super Investors</a>{' '}
            directory tracks a curated set of well-known Indian investors. Filing names (including trusts,
            HUFs, and corporate vehicles) are mapped to profiles using alias lists, manual curation, and
            automated entity-resolution rules. We avoid aggressive fuzzy matching that could attribute
            holdings to the wrong person. Portfolio values use quarter-end prices where available from
            our holdings pipeline.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900 dark:text-white">SAST (Substantial Acquisition of Shares)</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            SAST disclosures on NSE/BSE report when an acquirer crosses regulatory thresholds (e.g. 2%,
            5%, 10%). These filings supplement quarterly SHP data and can surface stake changes between
            quarter ends. IPOFins ingests SAST where available as an additional signal feed alongside SHP.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900 dark:text-white">Update Frequency</h2>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 ml-1">
            <li>IPO subscription and status data — refreshed on a regular pipeline schedule</li>
            <li>Mutual fund NAV — daily from AMFI</li>
            <li>Monthly holdings — after AMC portfolio disclosures are published</li>
            <li>Shareholding pattern &amp; super-investor portfolios — after NSE/BSE quarterly SHP filings are processed</li>
            <li>SAST disclosures — as published on exchanges</li>
            <li>Calculators — run entirely in your browser; no server-side storage</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900 dark:text-white">Limitations</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Data may be delayed, incomplete, or contain parsing errors despite validation checks.
            Always verify critical figures on official AMC, exchange, or regulatory websites before
            investing. See our{' '}
            <a href="/disclaimer" class="text-primary-600 dark:text-primary-400 hover:underline">disclaimer</a>{' '}
            for full legal terms.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="pt-4 border-t border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-700">
          <p class="text-sm text-surface-500 dark:text-surface-400">
            Spot an error? Email{' '}
            <a href="mailto:info@ipofins.com" class="text-primary-600 dark:text-primary-400 hover:underline">info@ipofins.com</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
